            {
              "id": "F2",
              "kind": "claimed_speedup",
              "family": "Repeated attribute reads on many Requirement instances (slots make attribute lookup faster and reduce per‑object memory).",
              "why": "The diff adds ``__slots__``; slots eliminate the per‑instance ``__dict__`` and make attribute access a direct C‑array lookup. Code that creates many Requirement objects and then reads their fields (name, extras, specifier, url, marker) will benefit.",
              "size_meaning": "Number of Requirement objects created; each object has a modestly sized extras set (≈ n/2 items) so the workload grows with *n*.",
              "make_source": "def make(n):\n    # Produce *n* requirement strings that parse successfully.\n    # Each string gets a name, a specifier, and ~n/2 extras to keep the\n    # objects non‑trivial while staying deterministic.\n    base = \"pkg\"\n    specs = [\"==1.0\", \">=2.0\", \"!=3.0\"]\n    extras_pool = [f\"extra{i}\" for i in range(max(1, n//2))]\n    out = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        name = f\"{base}{i}\"\n        specifier = specs[i % len(specs)]\n        extras = \",\".join(extras_pool[: (i % len(extras_pool)) + 1])\n        req = f\"{name}[{extras}]{specifier}\"\n        out.append([req])\n    return out",
              "example_args": [
                [
                  "pkg0[extra0]==1.0"
                ],
                [
                  "pkg1[extra0,extra1]>=2.0"
                ]
              ],
              "origin": "plan",
              "screen_ratio": 0.9868666927862122,
              "valid_fraction": 1.0,
              "error": null
            },
            {
              "id": "F3",
