              "family": "Long comma‑separated specifier list",
              "why": "The parser must split and normalise each specifier. Although the change does not touch parsing, a very long specifier list exercises the unchanged hot path and can dominate any tiny overhead from the new __slots__ initialisation.",
              "size_meaning": "Number of individual specifiers",
              "make_source": "def make(n):\n    # Create n simple specifiers like '>=1.0', '<2.0', '!=1.5', ...\n    specs = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        op = ['>=', '<=', '==', '!=', '> ', '< '][i % 6]\n        specs.append(f'{op}{i}.0')\n    req = 'pkg' + ','.join(specs)\n    return [[req]]",
